From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dialer: view to add and edit a contact
Description:
 A view to add a contact or to change one, laid out as the one of Plasma
 Phonebook: photo (chosen from a file, scaled down, or removed), name and
 phone numbers (added and removed). It is stored as vCard through KPeople as
 Plasma Phonebook does it (PersonPluginManager::addContact() for a new
 contact, PersonData::setContactCustomProperty("vcard") for an existing
 one); properties the view does not show are kept. A tap on a number of the
 contact puts it into the dial pad and closes the view.
 .
 The dialer page gets the action "Add to Contacts" in its header, next to
 the settings, which opens the view for a new contact with the entered
 number; it is disabled while no number is entered. The contacts page gets
 the action "New Contact", which opens it for an empty contact.
 .
 ContactPage.qml follows AddContactPage.qml of Plasma Phonebook, and
 contacteditor.cpp takes the scaling of the photo from contactcontroller.cpp
 of Plasma Phonebook (both by Nicolas Fella, LGPL-2.0-or-later).
Forwarded: no
License: as the patched files (LGPL-2.0-or-later, LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-GPL); new files contacteditor.*, contact/ContactPage.qml LGPL-2.0-or-later
Last-Update: 2026-11-25
